{
  "abstract": "For every N, we construct a determinant-detecting Chow point on the 21-fold power of the Fermat degree-two K3 surface whose completed relative Chow image ideal contains no nonzero term through order N in any of the 19 polarized period directions. The construction starts from an oriented rank-17 order-six K3 family with a relative determinant cycle, changes polarization using actual symplectic automorphisms of the Fermat surface, and selects O(N^17) re-polarized two-plane germs by exact polynomial interpolation. A 22-slot contraction gives branch inputs of degree O(N^88). Central rational-equivalence and graph-cut constructions match their actual Fermat values at degree O(N^105), while weighted linkage gives geometrically integral generic branch cycles at degree O(N^2205). The result is conditional on the relative source cycle and concerns the local image ideal at a Chow point. It does not supply a compatible Artin-neighbourhood lift, a dominating Chow component, or algebraicity of the determinant for a generic Picard-one K3.",
